# Code style

If a shorter version is clear on the first read, use that.

## TypeScript

Product types come from `shared/domain.ts`. A category is `CategoryId`, not `string`. HTTP and JSON input stays `unknown` until `shared/codec.ts` accepts it. No `any`. No `as` to silence a check. `as const` on a real tuple is fine.

A missing trip, proposal, flight, stay, or error is `null`. `undefined` only where a platform type has a hole: a missing array element, or the previous value of a Vue watch. Do not add `| undefined` to a domain value, and do not default a prop to `undefined`.

## Functions

A function calculates and returns a new value. It does not change the object it received.

```ts
function costPerPerson(totalCents: number, peopleCount: number): number {
  return Math.round(totalCents / peopleCount);
}
```

No classes, except `BadInput` and `NotFound`. No functional libraries, pipes, or monads. `map` and `filter` are enough.

Side effects stay at the edges: writing rows in the trip repository, answering a request, updating Vue view state. Totals and labels stay in `core/money.ts`, `core/present.ts`, and `format.ts`.

## Names

The name says what is inside, or what the function does. Do not use `data`, `item`, `temp`, `res`, or `val` when a domain word exists.

```ts
const pricedProposals = proposals.filter((proposal) => proposal.priced);
const cheapestTotal = Math.min(...pricedProposals.map((proposal) => proposal.totals.total));
```

A function starts with a verb: `formatMoney`, `presentTripSummary`. A boolean starts with `is` or `has`: `isPriced`, `hasProposals`.

## Simple

A function does one thing. If the name needs an explanation, rename it. Do not extract a helper that is used once. Do not add a layer "for later".

## Vue and CSS

`<script setup lang="ts">`. Props and emits are typed. A prop that every screen passes is required. Do not `v-model` into a trip, proposal, or line that came from the API.

Colors, type, space, radius, shadow, and layout sizes live in `fe/src/styles/tokens.css`. Use those variables. Space, type, radius, and layout sizes are `rem`. A hairline border is `1px`. The base style is the phone; a wider layout uses `@media (min-width: …)`, at `40rem` then `56rem`. The same rules are in `AGENTS.md`.
